  "notes": "Cortland uses a modified cash basis (recorded as cash). Governmental lines from Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances - Cash Basis, Total Governmental Funds 2025 column (Exhibit E, labels p5, totals column p6); beginning/ending cash = beginning/ending fund balance 685,085 / 807,780. Principal paid (25,000) and interest paid (13,075) on liabilities are printed below total expenditures under other financing sources (uses), recorded as disbursements with outside_printed_total. Debt service 21,798 in Debt Service fund (split not printed) recorded as debt service (principal and interest combined). Taxes 283,073 not broken down anywhere, kept as taxes (unlabeled). Business-type lines from Exhibit H total column (p8): printed total receipts 286,424 = operating receipts only; total disbursements 311,572 = operating disbursements/depreciation; interest paid 19,535 (non-operating) recorded as outside_printed_total disbursement; transfers in 25,421 in business_type.transfers_net; net position 165,558 -> 146,296 reconciles. Balance sheet uses Exhibit A Totals 2025 (governmental + business-type). Detail: nonmajor combining schedule (Schedule 4, pp10-11; Keno fund all zeros except fund balance 3,805, so omitted; zero lines omitted), plus Schedule 5 (budget summary by fund, p12) lines for every fund no other schedule covers: Special Revenue (Street), Debt Service and Proprietary Utility funds. Schedule 5's 'General' line (429,372 / 304,550) is not recorded: it combines General + Fire + the nonmajor funds (incl. transfers), so it would double count the Schedule 4 nonmajor lines and cannot be separated by fund from that page. Schedule 5 lines that include transfers or debt payments are split using the basic statements (split_from): Special Revenue receipts 140,666 = revenues 121,217 + transfers in 19,449; Special revenue disbursements 142,976 = expenditures 104,901 + principal 25,000 + interest 13,075 (Exhibit E p5); Utility funds receipts 311,845 = operating receipts 286,424 + transfers in 25,421 (Exhibit H p8); Utility funds disbursements 304,907 = operating payments 176,934 + capital purchases 38,438 + principal 70,000 + interest 19,535 (Exhibit I p9). Budget amounts are kept on the main part of each split line. Schedule 5 grand totals mix governmental and business-type funds, so the per-fund printed lines are used as detail_totals. Attempt 3 (verifier fix): added Street Special Revenue and Debt Service Schedule 5 lines; utility receipts line category set to Utility Charges; utility disbursements line split into operating, capital outlay and debt service. Read pages 1-12 of 12"
}
